all, frosted tree) act as bounce surfaces, lifting shadow side of the face with a warm fill. Light bouncing off the white fur hood softly brightens the upper cheeks and under-chin.\n  - Specular layer: gentle and diffuse. Skin shows pearly soft-rolloff highlight on forehead, nose bridge, and upper cheekbones — broad, low-intensity, no sharp pinpoint. Lips show a soft sheen. Eye catchlights are present but soft, suggesting a large diffused source.\n  - Transmitted/scatter layer: hair translucency is visible where the ambient frontal source grazes the dark strands — soft warm rim, not a hard backlit halo.\n  - Shadow layer: shadows are LIFTED and ambient-filled. The cast shadow on the wall behind the subject is soft-edged, medium-gray, and contains internal tonal variation rather than being a flat dark shape. No pure black voids anywhere in the frame.\n- Portrait lighting pattern: the soft frontal even illumination most closely resembles a clamshell/soft beauty setup or a window-softbox frontal, but the small directional component produces a faint loop pattern — the nose shadow is barely visible and soft, angled slightly downward toward the viewer's left mouth corner. Not Rembrandt, not split, not strong butterfly. The face is overall evenly lit with very gentle cheekbone modeling.\n- Practical lights: the Christmas tree contributes multiple small warm practical light points in the background (blurred to soft round bokeh discs) plus a faint pinkish glow on the surrounding fur trim and wall.\n- Atmospheric interaction: subtle haze/softness in the air gives a gentle glow around the brighter points (tree lights, decorative glass in foreground). No visible fog or smoke.\n- Specular behavior: pearly soft-rolloff across skin, glossy lip sheen, glass-like highlights on the crystal candy-dish in foreground (sharp specular reflections on curved glass), satin-like soft highlights on the white fur trim.",
